---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_URL } from '../consts';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'About', url: `${SITE_URL}/about/` },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About NSN Explorer: Free Government Parts Data"
  description="NSN Explorer is a free, independent index of U.S. government parts solicitations and prices built from public DIBBS, SAM.gov and USAspending records."
  pageType="AboutPage"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    NSN Explorer is an independent project built for suppliers who want to find and win federal
    parts work — it indexes public U.S. government procurement records — DIBBS solicitations and
    awards, and USAspending contract data — into one searchable site.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <p class="gloss">
    We built it because that data exists but is scattered across systems built for procurement
    officers, not for the businesses that could fill the orders. NSN Explorer renders the same
    public facts clearly: what's open now, per part, over time, with a link back to the source
    record behind every figure — so a supplier can find work and quote it with confidence. The
    same index also serves buyers sizing up a category, researchers and market-watchers tracking
    federal demand, investors watching a sector, and journalists checking a number.
  </p>
  <p class="gloss">
    We are not a government entity and we don't sell parts to the government ourselves on this
    site, and we don't broker or submit bids on anyone's behalf. Every figure here links to the
    public record it came from. Nothing on this site is estimated or modeled — if you find an
    error, tell us and we'll fix it.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <p class="gloss">NSN Explorer is operated by NAO Parts LLC.</p>

  <p class="gloss">
    Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
